  user_input {
    user_response: "Analyze the attached HTML file and convert it into a functional reviewer/exam application.\n\nRequirements:\n- Use ONLY HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript.\n- Do NOT use React, Next.js, Vue, Angular, npm packages, or build tools.\n- Keep everything in a single self-contained HTML file.\n\nFeatures:\n1. Display only ONE question at a time.\n2. Make answer choices clickable.\n3. Save selected answers when navigating between questions.\n4. Add Previous and Next buttons.\n5. Show progress (e.g. Question 5 of 100 + progress bar).\n6. Add a question navigator panel showing answered/unanswered questions.\n7. Add a Submit button at the end.\n8. After submission:\n   - Calculate score\n   - Show correct answers\n   - Highlight correct answers in green\n   - Highlight incorrect answers in red\n   - Show final percentage\n9. Save progress using localStorage.\n10. Make the UI mobile responsive.\n11. Add keyboard shortcuts:\n    - Left Arrow = Previous\n    - Right Arrow = Next\n    - Number Keys = Select Choice\n12. Add Dark Mode toggle.\n13. Add Shuffle Questions and Shuffle Choices functionality.\n14. Add Review Incorrect Answers mode.\n\nRefactor the existing Google Forms export as much as possible:\n- Extract all questions and choices into a JavaScript data structure.\n- Remove unnecessary Google Forms scripts, styles, tracking code, and generated markup.\n- Render questions dynamically using JavaScript.\n\nImportant:\n- Preserve all questions and answer choices from the original file.\n- Do not lose any content.\n- Produce production-ready code.\n- Return the complete updated HTML file, not pseudocode."
    items {
      text: "Analyze the attached HTML file and convert it into a functional reviewer/exam application.\n\nRequirements:\n- Use ONLY HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript.\n- Do NOT use React, Next.js, Vue, Angular, npm packages, or build tools.\n- Keep everything in a single self-contained HTML file.\n\nFeatures:\n1. Display only ONE question at a time.\n2. Make answer choices clickable.\n3. Save selected answers when navigating between questions.\n4. Add Previous and Next buttons.\n5. Show progress (e.g. Question 5 of 100 + progress bar).\n6. Add a question navigator panel showing answered/unanswered questions.\n7. Add a Submit button at the end.\n8. After submission:\n   - Calculate score\n   - Show correct answers\n   - Highlight correct answers in green\n   - Highlight incorrect answers in red\n   - Show final percentage\n9. Save progress using localStorage.\n10. Make the UI mobile responsive.\n11. Add keyboard shortcuts:\n    - Left Arrow = Previous\n    - Right Arrow = Next\n    - Number Keys = Select Choice\n12. Add Dark Mode toggle.\n13. Add Shuffle Questions and Shuffle Choices functionality.\n14. Add Review Incorrect Answers mode.\n\nRefactor the existing Google Forms export as much as possible:\n- Extract all questions and choices into a JavaScript data structure.\n- Remove unnecessary Google Forms scripts, styles, tracking code, and generated markup.\n- Render questions dynamically using JavaScript.\n\nImportant:\n- Preserve all questions and answer choices from the original file.\n- Do not lose any content.\n- Produce production-ready code.\n- Return the complete updated HTML file, not pseudocode."
    }
    media {
      mime_type: "text/html"
      blobref {
        blob_id: "/blobstore/prod/makersuite/spanner_managed/global::000054e2ea70026d:0000015f:2:000054e2ea70026d:0000000000000001::fa222703d40102b1:000002118d1018bc:00065551d1ea142f"
      }
      uri: "Master\'s Mastery Test_ SPDI Set A.html"
    }
  }
}
