    thinking: "**Considering Modular Structure**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag: the token limit. My question list is extensive, and a single output file risks exceeding the constraints. I\'m now exploring a modular structure, hoping it will let me avoid that, and make it easier for me.\n\n\n**Exploring File Structure**\n\nI\'ve hit a better idea! I should write the questions into a `/src/questions.js` file and import it using a script tag in the `index.html` file. This is client-side, vanilla JS/HTML, which fits all the criteria, and it also avoids exceeding the token limit by splitting the work! First, I\'ll create `/src/questions.js` with the questions data. After that, I will be able to write the beautiful and responsive `index.html` file that uses it!\n\n\n**Compiling Questions List**\n\nI\'m now writing `/src/questions.js`, striving for maximum compactness to minimize token usage. I\'ve started listing all 53 questions with their choices and correct answers, focusing on efficiency and brevity in the JSON structure. My current focus is to balance completeness with token optimization.\n\n\n**Adding More Questions**\n\nI\'ve added four more questions to the list in `/src/questions.js`, striving for the best combination of brevity and completeness in the JSON format. The current questions are about tuberculation in pipes, Transite pipes, the order of ejector pump components, and deluge fire sprinkler systems. My goal is to add more questions and finalize the format.\n\n\n**Expanding Question Data**\n\nI\'ve added six more questions to `/src/questions.js`, maintaining conciseness in the JSON structure. Now I have new questions about travel distance, pipe standards, PPR, vents, and packing materials. I\'m aiming for a good diversity of questions in this round.\n\n\n**Finalizing Questions Database**\n\nI\'ve finished adding questions to the `/src/questions.js` file, reaching a total of nineteen. This round included questions about caulk joints, scrub sinks, stainless steel types, ozone, jet pumps, and PPR connections. I think this database covers a very good variety of key topics!\n\n\n**Defining Pipe Production**\n\nI\'m now adding four more questions to `/src/questions.js`, focusing on various aspects of plumbing and pipe systems. Included are questions on seamless pipes, manifolds, flowing artesian wells, and the terminus of a loop vent. I\'m aiming for a good mix of topics.\n\n\n**Adding More Questions**\n\nI\'ve added five more questions to `/src/questions.js`, maintaining conciseness in the JSON structure. My most recent questions are about the detention time in a septic tank, a bushing, a hygrometer, the air pressure test, and ideal valves for throttling. I\'m focusing on ensuring these questions align with the established format.\n\n\n**Adding Valve and Fitting Questions**\n\nI\'ve added six more questions to `/src/questions.js`, maintaining conciseness in the JSON structure. Now I have new questions about different valve types, flood level, hotel lavatory hot water demand, phase transitions, and fitting types.\n\n\n**Adding More Questions**\n\nI\'ve added four more questions to the list in `/src/questions.js`, focusing on various aspects of plumbing and water treatment systems. The new questions are about Chemical Oxygen Demand, sludge in a septic tank, the Jar Test, and receptors. I am aiming to finalize the question set soon.\n\n\n**Adding More Questions**\n\nI\'ve added five more questions to `/src/questions.js`, maintaining conciseness in the JSON structure. Now I have new questions about hose bibbs, water sample volumes, PVC pipe lengths, jockey pumps, and viscosity. My focus now is ensuring the format\'s consistency.\n\n\n**Adding More Questions**\n\nI\'ve added five more questions to `/src/questions.js`, maintaining conciseness in the JSON structure. Now I\'m focused on finishing the question set. I\'ve added questions on area drains, brass pipe alloys, pressure reducing valves, malleability, and soil pipe weight.\n\n\n**Adding Final Questions**\n\nI\'ve added the last five questions to `/src/questions.js`, maintaining conciseness in the JSON structure. My final questions cover therms, WSFU of bedpan washers, hanger rod sizes, cone of depression in water tables, and the source of drinking water criteria. I\'m now done with the question database!\n\n\n\n**Adding Image Questions**\n\nI\'ve just added the final six questions to `/src/questions.js`. I focused on adding image-based questions about sprinkler types and valve components, plus SI units of temperature and the Provincial Water Utilities Act. The questions are complete, so now I can start writing the HTML and JS components.\n\n\n\n**Adding More Questions**\n\nI\'ve added the last few questions to the database! I covered topics like a sacrificial rod in water heaters, backflow critical levels, horsepower conversions, atmospheric oxygen percentage, and green building code water reserve. Now the questions are complete, so I will start designing the overall presentation using HTML and JavaScript.\n\n\n**Defining Questions**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the `/src/questions.js` file, adding the final questions. I\'ve included questions on barometric loops and the purpose of a water hammer arrestor. With the questions complete, I can move on to the `index.html` and accompanying JavaScript code.\n\n\n**Defining Questions**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the `/src/questions.js` file. I added questions related to the required vent stack extension, a Level 2 water service, the minimum vent size for a water closet, the process of heat transfer in fluid motion, and the extension of the soil or waste stack above the highest horizontal drain connected to the stack. With these, I believe I have a thorough question set.\n\n\n"
