  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the index.html**\n\nI\'ve got good news! I\'ve just finished the `/src/questions.js` database. My next task involves crafting the `/index.html` file, which will import the question database. The focus is to design a full review application, complete with all necessary elements.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nOkay, I\'ve outlined the core features for `/index.html`. My vision includes a professional, responsive layout with a dark mode toggle. I\'m focusing on local storage synchronization, question shuffling, key bindings, and search/filter functionality. Crucially, I\'m integrating a \"Review Incorrect Answers\" mode for targeted study. Vite compatibility is also a primary concern, and it\'s looking like loading `/src/questions.js` with a relative path will work.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the master self-contained `/index.html` file. It imports the `/src/questions.js` script and implements the complete client-side reviewer application with an off-white Slate/Indigo visual design, dark mode, keyboard controls, progress indicators, interactive quiz logic, score summary, local storage persistence, search filters, and an incorrect-answer targeted review mode."
