  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Extracting Styling Information**\n\nOkay, here\'s the current state of my analysis. I am focusing on extracting the core styling elements from the \"Professional Polish\" design, like colors, fonts, spacing, and layout, and filtering out the rest. Specifically, I need to be careful to avoid restructuring or removing content, but instead, only address styling.\n\n\n**Analyzing Color Palette**\n\nI am now delving into the color palette of \"Professional Polish.\" I\'ve begun mapping the theme\'s colors to Tailwind config extensions. My approach involves defining custom color variables and replacing existing references, specifically focusing on `indigo-600` with `brand-600`. I\'m also considering what goes into the style section.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now making refinements to the visual elements. I\'ve been examining the current `body` styling, and I\'m updating it to use the new color scheme. I\'m also considering styling the top decorative bar, aiming for a high-contrast aesthetic that fits the \"Professional Polish\" design. I\'m choosing a clean, consistent color over the rainbow gradient or a `var(--primary)` style, as it\'s cleaner. I\'m focusing on consistency with the overall visual direction.\n\n\n**Updating Visual Cohesion**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Professional Polish\" theme colors. I\'m styling the award icon\'s background using the brand\'s primary color, aiming for a consistent and professional look. I\'ve also decided to make the top decoration bar a solid primary blue for enhanced visual cohesion within the overall aesthetic. I\'m focusing on ensuring all elements align with the design\'s professional feel.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing the latest styling refinements. I\'ve updated a few of the visual components, such as the thin top decoration to have a specific height of `1` and a solid background color, and adjusted the Header class to include a bottom border and specific background and blur styles. I\'ve also updated the award icon wrapper, ensuring it echoes the \"E\" block style, and customized the shortcuts-helper panel\'s background and border colors.\n\n\n**Implementing Style Transitions**\n\nI\'ve just finished implementing style transitions for a \"welcome card\" and other informational labels. Specifically, I\'ve updated the background, border, and blur styles of the \"welcome card\" to more closely match the dark theme, using the slate color palette, and replaced the hardcoded indigo values to use the new color scheme. I also transitioned the progress bar section to the slate-based styling. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual coherence across all elements.\n\n\n**Refining Element Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the styling of several elements. I\'ve updated the container block to incorporate specific background, border, and shadow styles, ensuring it matches the design\'s HTML. I\'m also transitioning the inner content\'s text and colors for better visual consistency. My goal is to achieve an exact style match.\n\n\n**Styling Visual Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating new styling elements. I\'ve updated the answered-indicator to use `text-[#2563eb] dark:text-[#3b82f6]`. For the progress bar, I\'ve defined styles for the track and fill, incorporating colors and rounded corners. My focus now is on integrating these color-specific updates.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Styling**\n\nI\'m now styling the question card, focusing on implementing the container, label badge, points display, and question title using the specified Tailwind classes. I\'ve updated the question container, incorporated styles for the question index label badge, adjusted the question points styling, and refined the question title. I\'m also now examining the Navigation Buttons section to assess further styling needs.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Buttons**\n\nI\'m now refining the navigation buttons to align with the design\'s crisp look. I\'ve updated the button styles, focusing on precise padding, rounded corners, border colors, background states, and text colors. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency across both the previous and next buttons, as well as refining the hover state.\n\n\n**Adjusting Button Styles**\n\nI\'m now adjusting the button style within the form finalize block. I\'m focusing on the current styles used for the \"submit\" button and refining them to align with the overall design. I\'m particularly evaluating the background and hover states to enhance visual coherence and consistency. I also checked its padding and rounded corners, to provide some additional adjustments.\n\n\n**Updating Visual Cohesion**\n\nI\'m now adapting the finalize block and sidebar settings to the style specifications. For the finalize block, I\'ve implemented the provided Tailwind classes for background, border, padding, and button styling. I\'ve also integrated the submit button\'s specifications for background, hover state, and text. I\'ve updated the sidebar container and header to match the color specifications.\n\n\n**Integrating Theme Adjustments**\n\nI\'m now integrating more theme-specific adjustments. I have updated settings icon using the appropriate color classes, and the toggle sliders with the theme\'s colors, replacing the old `indigo` values. I am also planning on working on the search bar.\n\n\n**Refining Search Bar Style**\n\nI am now focusing on the search bar. I have updated the container with `bg-white dark:bg-[#1e293b]`, a rounded `xl` corner radius, appropriate padding, and a border and shadow. The input field\'s styling includes size adjustments, rounded corners, focus states, and color theme integration. I\'ve also incorporated styles for the search icon. Next, I will be working on the Question Navigator Grid Card.\n\n\n**Styling Navigator Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on styling the Question Navigator Grid Card. I\'ve updated the card container to match the design with specific background, border, shadow, and spacing. I\'ve updated the styles for the grid icon to ensure the text colors are consistent with other design elements. I\'ve also integrated the nav count badge with corresponding background and text styles, ensuring it uses the theme colors. I\'m focusing on ensuring these elements contribute to the overall visual cohesion.\n\n\n**Updating Navigation Buttons**\n\nI\'m now incorporating specific styling for the question navigation buttons, building upon recent refinements. I am updating the styles for answered, unanswered, correct, and incorrect states to align with the \"Professional Polish\" design. I\'m focusing on exact color matches and using Tailwind classes to achieve the desired visual look. I am reviewing the specific code for the `renderNavigator()` function to precisely edit the elements to reflect the button styles.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Styles**\n\nI\'m now making final adjustments to the navigation button styles based on design specifications. I\'ve updated the styles for answered and unanswered states to precisely match the \"Professional Polish\" design, specifically changing `bg-indigo-600` for more specific classes to include the correct colors and borders. I\'m also ensuring the correct active button style is maintained.\n\n\n**Implementing Active Navigation Styles**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final changes for the navigation buttons based on the most recent design input. My latest refinement involves setting up active states. I am setting the \"active\" style to `bg-[#2563eb] text-white border-[#2563eb]`, which matches the current state of the design. I\'ve also incorporated the correct handling of `isCurrent` and `isGraded` to ensure an elegant visual state.\n\n\n**Styling Choice Elements**\n\nI\'m now styling the choice elements within `renderActiveQuestion()`, focusing on the button\'s appearance and the prefix badge. I\'ve defined styles for the button, including width, text alignment, padding, and rounded corners, and also incorporated border and transition effects. I\'m also addressing the text size and font weight for a clean look. Next, I\'ll be working on visual states.\n\n\n**Adjusting Choice Visuals**\n\nI\'m now styling the choice elements to ensure they have the proper visual look. I\'ve updated the button\'s visual states for both selected and unselected options. For selected choices, I\'m setting the background, border, and badge colors, incorporating color transitions. I\'ve also implemented corresponding styles for unselected choices, with appropriate hover effects. I am making these states specific and clear.\n\n\n**Enhancing Choice Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating the radio dot indicator and badge into the choice elements. I\'ve created the visual element, defining styles for the radio circle container and text and the letter badge to match the design. I\'m focusing on ensuring these additions contribute to a professional and polished appearance.\n\n\n**Integrating Choice Prefixes**\n\nI\'m now integrating the letter badge prefix and exploring button states for choice elements. I\'ve designed the letter badge as a circular element and styled the active state of the choice button, defining its appearance. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual feedback for selected choices.\n\n\n**Verifying Button States**\n\nI\'m now meticulously verifying the button states within the `renderActiveQuestion()` function to ensure they perfectly match the \"Professional Polish\" theme. Specifically, I\'m reviewing the graded states, including the correct and incorrect visual feedback, to make certain the styling transitions are seamless. My focus is on achieving a polished and user-friendly experience.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual styling, specifically for the graded icon elements in choice buttons. I\'ve introduced specific classes and corresponding attributes for correct and incorrect choices, including background, border, and badge colors for correct choices. I\'m focusing on ensuring clear visual feedback for both correct and incorrect answers and integrating lucide icons.\n\n\n**Finalizing Feedback Styling**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the feedback visuals. I\'m styling correct and incorrect answer feedback with success and danger colors, transitioning the design for seamless visual clarity. I\'m also implementing a muted background for unselected, incorrect choices, improving the user experience. I am checking the Answer Feedback and Reset Confirm panels to verify the application of the chosen styles.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
