  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Main Structure**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the structural integrity. The core container utilizes `max-w-7xl`, `mx-auto`, and padding. Inside is a single `div` element, employing a grid with a single column on smaller screens, expanding to twelve columns on larger displays, with a gap of 8. I\'m focusing on wrapping the active exam container with an ID.\n\n\n**Implementing Visibility Control**\n\nI\'m now integrating an \"exam-workspace\" identifier to control display based on exam state. I\'ve pinpointed line 136 for modification. Replacing the current `<main>` structure with a `start-screen` div, and applying visual styling to match the rest of the application.\n\n\n**Refining Content Presentation**\n\nI\'m now assessing the visual elements within the start screen\'s grid. I\'m focusing on the presentation of exam details. I\'m noting the use of `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3` for responsiveness. I\'ll need to confirm the use of text color and size, and overall visual balance.\n\n\n**Evaluating Visual Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of visual styling within the start screen\'s grid elements. I\'m taking a close look at the text elements, specifically, the `text-emerald` and `dark:text-emerald` styles for the percentage display, and also, the styling for the time selector in detail. I\'m focusing on color, size, and font weight to achieve visual harmony, with a goal of presenting a very nice display.\n\n\n\n**Assessing Exam Instructions**\n\nI\'m now integrating exam instructions into the start screen. I\'ve noted a structured display for duration selection with an \"Unlimited\" option. Also, I\'m examining the visual treatment of the instructions and rules section. I\'m focusing on the clarity of presentation, including list styling, and the overall layout for readability. I am also working on the design and presentation of the \"info\" icon.\n\n\n**Refining Button Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the button interactions within the start screen. I\'m focusing on the \"Reset Progress\" and \"Start Exam\" buttons. I\'ve noted the styling, particularly the use of `rose-500` and `blue-500` colors and shadow effects. I will be sure to integrate the appropriate event handlers, and will test the interactions and transitions for a smooth experience. I am examining the inclusion of lucide icons for visual clarity. I am focusing on their respective IDs for referencing.\n\n\n**Confirming Element Placement**\n\nI\'m now verifying the correct placement for the closing `</div>` of the `exam-workspace`. I\'ve confirmed line 348 marks the end of the workspace grid. I\'m now integrating the new `</div>` placement. I also need to place the timer in a prominent header location, analyzing the header structure for optimal placement. I can use the header control structure for proper integration.\n\n\n**Integrating Timer Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the timer display and functionality into the application header, before the theme toggle. I\'m focusing on crafting the visual style using Tailwind classes, with a hidden, flex layout that uses a light background and border. I plan on making the timer visible depending on the state of the exam, which I will test.\n\n\n**Adding Timer Card Placement**\n\nI\'m now integrating a prominent timer display in the right sidebar. I\'m focusing on adding a \"Timer Status\" card above the \"Exam Settings\" card. I\'ve located the appropriate insertion point and I\'ll use the given HTML structure to build a visual timer display. I will design this to provide a highly visible countdown and warning indicators for better time management. I\'ll test to ensure it is always visible.\n\n\n**Refining Timer Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating the timer\'s visual components within the sidebar\'s timer card. I\'ve designed a clear time display and active status badge. I\'m focusing on the timer progress bar and will ensure a clear and user friendly display of the time remaining. I\'ve focused on ensuring the visual contrast works.\n\n\n"
