    thinking: "**Drafting Variable Declarations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how best to structure our Javascript updates. Specifically, I\'m thinking about variable declarations. It seems logical to place these right above the `// Settings` section for clarity. I\'ve started drafting some examples, like `examStarted` and `timerDuration`, just to get a feel for the placement and structure.\n\n\n**Refining Exam State Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the logic related to exam state variables, especially in relation to local storage. I\'m focusing on scenarios where an exam is \"graded\" (completed and under review) and how that impacts the start screen and timer behavior. Specifically, I\'m working through how `examStarted`, `isGraded` and `timerDuration` interact, making sure they correctly reflect whether the user is taking an exam, reviewing a finished one, or starting fresh. I\'m also ensuring the start screen and workspace are displayed correctly in all cases.\n\n\n**Implementing Timer Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the timer updates. I need to make the ticker beautiful and robust. I\'m focusing on the time format (HH:MM:SS), dynamically updating the progress bar, and dynamic styling alerts when time is low. Additionally, I\'m integrating automatic submission on time expiration. I\'ve also added handling for unlimited mode, hiding the header timer and displaying \"Unlimited\" instead. I\'m also ensuring the timer correctly reflects how many questions exist.\n\n\n**Finalizing Timer Logic**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the timer logic. I\'m focusing on ensuring it handles all edge cases. I\'ve been testing the integration with auto-submission, making certain the countdown is smooth and seamless across different scenarios. I\'m also ensuring the unlimited mode is gracefully handled, hiding the timer, as expected. The progress bar update and dynamic styling are integrated and tested.\n\n\n**Formatting Time Remaining**\n\nI\'m now making final updates to the time remaining updates. I am focusing on formatting the duration for the timer, and integrating the progress bar calculations. I\'ve also incorporated the urgent coloring logic, ensuring the timer badge changes color appropriately. I\'m focusing on ensuring it looks beautiful and clean.\n\n\n**Styling Timer Alerts**\n\nI\'m now styling the timer alerts, making it visually intuitive for users. I\'m focusing on the \"urgent coloring logic\" for the timer badge and progress bar. The logic now triggers a red and flashing alert for the last minute, and amber for the last five minutes, dynamically updating classes for a more appealing and clear user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Timer Styling**\n\nI\'m now refining the timer styling based on time remaining, and integrated it with the countdown update function. I\'ve standardized styling the progress bar, header timer, and badge. I\'ve ensured a blue styling when the exam is active. The logic for urgent coloring, triggering amber for the last five minutes and red for the final minute, is in place.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view lines 910 to 975 of `index.html` to examine the full submission logic and see how we can trigger or integrate our timer submission path."
