    thinking: "**Positioning Timer Functions**\n\nOkay, I\'ve identified the insertion point for the timer functions. Specifically, I\'ll be placing them directly after the `lucide.createIcons()` call within the `init()` function. My next steps involve detailed design and implementation of these timer functions, I am excited to make sure they are flawless.\n\n\n**Implementing Exam Timer Function**\n\nI\'ve just finished the `startExam` function, which handles exam initiation with a set duration. It manages exam state, timer duration, and local storage updates. I\'ve incorporated time calculations and storage for the end time, along with UI transitions. I also ensured lucide icons refresh after the screen switch.\n\n\n**Defining Clear-Progress Function**\n\nI\'ve just designed the `clearAllProgress` function. It\'s built to reset all user progress, encompassing clearing local storage entries such as answers, exam status, and timer information. It includes resetting state variables and ensuring any active timer intervals are cleared to avoid any unexpected issues. I\'ve also implemented hiding any post-submission related UI elements.\n\n\n**Refining Reset Button Action**\n\nI\'ve just added a confirmation feedback for the clear button. When pressed, the button text updates temporarily to confirm action completion with the updated text \"Progress Reset & Cache Cleared!\". I\'ve also implemented a timeout to revert to the original text after a brief delay.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'ve also started working on the timer ticker function. It now updates the remaining time and visual indicators in real-time, handling zero time with a clean reset. I am focusing on making the UI updates smooth. I also am making the timer appear.\n\n\n**Finalizing Timer UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for the timer. I\'ve integrated the time formatting logic. Specifically, I\'m displaying hours, minutes, and seconds. I also ensure the time updates the header and sidebar in real-time. Additionally, I\'m calculating the progress bar percentage and updating it dynamically. I also added in auto submission of the exam.\n\n\n**Styling Timer Alerts**\n\nI\'m now styling the timer\'s visual alerts. Specifically, if the time remaining goes below a minute, the progress bar turns red and flashes, with a critical badge. Between one and five minutes, it\'s amber. I\'ve ensured a smooth UI update and color coding.\n\n\n**Adding Timer Status Visuals**\n\nI\'ve just styled the timer visuals to indicate the exam\'s status. If less than a minute remains, the timer displays a flashing red progress bar with a critical badge. Between one and five minutes, it\'s amber. The rest of the time, the progress bar is normal and active, as well as the badge changing color, and I made sure the UI changes are smooth and clean.\n\n\n**Refining Timer State Control**\n\nI\'ve just been refining the control of the timer state. I have implemented a system to stop and clear the timer interval. I\'ve also added a means of hiding the timer\'s UI containers on demand. Finally, I\'m working to show a static \"SUBMITTED\" state in the timer after the exam is complete.\n\n\n**Updating Final Submission**\n\nI\'ve just added the final submission logic for when the timer expires. I\'ve set the progress bar to 100% and styled it green, along with the \"GRADED\" badge. I\'ve also incorporated an auto-submission function that\'s triggered when time runs out. I am working to ensure this automatically calls the submit button.\n\n\n**Avoiding Alert Popups**\n\nI\'m now implementing non-disruptive feedback. I\'m replacing `window.alert` with a dynamic banner within the Results modal to inform users of auto-submission due to time expiration. I\'ve located the Results modal elements in `index.html`. My plan is to add a banner space either below the circular progress indicator or at the top of the modal, displaying a message like \"Time Expired! Your exam was automatically submitted.\" to improve the user experience.\n\n\n"
