    modified_response: "I have successfully completed the implementation of the **Start Exam screen** and the dynamic **Countdown Timer** for the Master\'s Mastery Test reviewer application:\n\n### **Design & Visual Concept**\n*   **Professional Polish**: Designed a premium entry portal for the exam with a responsive dashboard layout, complete with an elegant SVG-enhanced certificate layout, custom typography selection, and vibrant accent colors.\n*   **Aesthetic Balance**: Wrapped the primary exam area in a responsive container, splitting real estate dynamically on desktop between the primary exam workspace and a cohesive, high-contrast right sidebar.\n\n---\n\n### **Implemented Key Modules**\n\n1.  **Start Exam Screen**:\n    *   **Dynamic Metadata**: Displays the live total number of questions fetched dynamically from the database (`76 Questions`) alongside selectable countdown durations.\n    *   **Configuration Hub**: Employs a stylized duration selector permitting custom-timed sessions (ranging from quick 15-minute mock sessions to comprehensive 180-minute full simulations) or a relaxing \"Unlimited Time\" study mode.\n    *   **Start & Reset Anchors**: Features a prominent, highly clickable **Start Exam** action button, alongside a secondary **Clear Saved Answers & Reset Cache** button to clear all historical answers and shuffle mapping parameters instantly.\n\n2.  **Robust Countdown Timer & Dynamic Indicators**:\n    *   **Multi-View HUD**: Updates both a compact header countdown indicator and an immersive sidebar timer card synchronously every second.\n    *   **Real-time Urgency Styling**:\n        *   *Standard State*: Clean slate/emerald styling with a modern tracking progress bar.\n        *   *Warning State (< 5 minutes left)*: Transitions visual themes to warning amber to denote impending limits.\n        *   *Critical State (< 1 minute left)*: Transitions progress indicators to an active, glowing crimson with high-visibility pulsing animations.\n\n3.  **Automatic Grading on Timeout**:\n    *   Handles zero-time limits by stopping the timer loops and automatically triggering the submission logic.\n    *   Displays a beautiful, non-disruptive **Time Limit Reached** warning banner inside the final circular-chart Results summary.\n\n4.  **Persistent Session Recovery**:\n    *   Maintains the active countdown, selected answers, current question indices, and exam state across accidental browser refreshes or tab-reloads using secure `localStorage` key-value mappings."
