  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Input Method**\n\nOkay, so I realized the search was fruitless. The user didn\'t upload a file. The HTML for the Google Form was actually pasted directly into the chat prompt, which I can verify by looking at the chat history!\n\n\n**Analyzing HTML Position**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a better handle on things now. I\'m focusing on the position of the HTML in the user\'s prompt. I confirmed it was pasted above the `</USER_REQUEST>` tag, which is key. Now I\'m working on analyzing the contents, and the size of the provided HTML to see if I can get to the bottom of the user\'s issue.\n\n\n**Extracting HTML Elements**\n\nOkay, the user provided a massive HTML block, which seems to contain the Google Form. I\'m focusing on parsing this HTML now. I\'ve realized it\'s accessible within the prompt\'s context. I can now extract the individual questions! I can see elements like `<div class=\"Qr7Oae\" role=\"listitem\">`. I\'m starting to carefully analyze the structure and contents within these \"listitem\" elements. I\'ve identified several questions, including those on iron fittings and abbreviations. I am working through reading those questions!\n\n\n**Identifying Plumbing Questions**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress by focusing on the specific content of these extracted list items! I can identify many questions that relate to plumbing. I\'m seeing questions like, \"What is the travel distance of the pipe given an offset length of 70 cm and an offset angle of 45\302\260?\", and \"What type of fire sprinkler system has open sprinkler heads, does not contain water or pressurized air, and activates all at once when a detector senses smoke or heat?\". I am carefully reading through them. It seems most questions are related to plumbing, not HTML parsing, so I\'m updating my approach!\n\n\n**Enumerating Plumbing Questions**\n\nI\'ve identified additional plumbing questions within the extracted content. I\'ve noted questions on connecting PPR pipes, the terminus of loop vents, and the characteristics of pipes derived from steel billets. I\'m also analyzing questions about various fittings, septic tank detention times, humidity measurement, air pressure substitution in water testing, throttling valves, fixture edges, hot water demand, and phase transitions of gases to solids. I\'m carefully reading through these questions. I can see the user wants the questions answered!\n\n\n**Reading Plumbing Questions**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the extracted plumbing questions and have added a few more to my list. I am now reading questions about the Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD) of water, sinkable solids in septic tanks, and jar testing. I am also working through the definition of an approved plumbing fixture, a fitting used to connect hoses, the volume of a water sample for total hardness testing, and the standard length of PVC pipe. I am also reading about fire protection system pumps and the concept of liquid viscosity. And finally, I\'ve got a question related to basement areaway floor drain assemblies.\n\n\n**Categorizing Plumbing Queries**\n\nI\'m now cataloging more questions. I\'m noting ones about brass pipe alloys, pressure-reducing valves, and material deformability. I\'m also considering soil pipe standards, heat measurement units, and bedpan washer WSFU. Additionally, I\'m identifying questions about hanger rod sizes, water table depressions, and drinking water quality criteria. And standpipe systems. I\'ve realized there are a lot more!\n\n\n**Listing Additional Plumbing Questions**\n\nI\'m still categorizing. I see questions about the Provincial Water Utilities Act of 1973, identifying valve parts and the role of a sacrificial anode rod. There\'s a question about critical level markings on backflow prevention devices and the horsepower equivalent. I also noted questions about atmospheric oxygen percentage, fire reserve percentages, external threads, sitz baths, and Orangeburg pipe. There is a question about hot water distribution systems, barometric loops, and water service levels. I have noted questions about water closet vents. There is a final question on heat transfer processes.\n\n\n**Verifying Question Count**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed that the HTML contains the list items I extracted, which matches the number of questions I previously identified. I see the HTML contains 76 questions, not 100 as the user expected. It seems the Google Form may be a partial test. I am now working on understanding why the discrepancy exists, because I know there can be 100 questions. I\'m investigating if it\'s a first part of a larger exam.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am going to search for common Philippine Master Plumber board exam questions for Sanitary, Plumbing, Drainage, and Installation (SPDI) to compile 24 high-quality, authentic additional questions with standard choices and correct answers."
