  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Image Handling**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. I was checking how the application handles choice-specific images, and I\'m puzzled. In question 25, the choices are A, B, C, D, but the `index.html` file lacks image rendering within the choice containers. The `choicesOrder.forEach` loop doesn\'t seem to address image elements. I must focus in on this!\n\n\n**Refining Image Integration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating images seamlessly into the choice buttons. I\'ve designed a rendering method for choice buttons: When `q.images` exists and `q.images[idx]` is available, I append an `<img>` element with classes `max-h-24 max-w-full rounded-md object-contain mb-2` inside the button, above the text and letter. This ensures a consistent and appealing display, fitting both desktop and mobile layouts. I am checking if there are some edge cases.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Implementation**\n\nI\'m verifying the image paths in the JavaScript data structure and confirming `q.images` availability. It looks like it exists! I\'m now examining the `choiceBtn` creation code, focusing on lines 1030-1044, to implement image insertion where appropriate. This includes ensuring correct image attributes and positioning within the choice buttons for seamless display. I\'m testing conditional rendering based on image availability.\n\n\n**Structuring Image Display**\n\nI\'m now structuring the choice buttons for optimal image display. If images are available, the button becomes a vertically stacked container. I\'m adding `headerWrap` to contain letter and text, and `imgWrap` for the image. The class name is updated too. I\'m using `flex flex-col items-start space-y-3` in the class name to achieve vertical stacking of elements.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Layout**\n\nI\'ve crafted a method to handle image displays within choice buttons! I\'m adding `imgWrap`, which contains an `img` element. I\'m adding classes, and conditional logic. I\'m setting the `src`, `alt` attributes, and other attributes to configure the display of the image, too! I\'ve also implemented conditional rendering and ensured a vertical stacking of elements if an image is available.\n\n```\n\n```\n\n**Examining Question Data**\n\nI\'m now investigating specific questions to check image representation and question types. I see that questions 54, 55, and 56 all use the same image, `unnamed(4).jpg`, even though they identify different sprinkler types. I\'m also looking for questions related to \"bulb\" within the data files to understand how those are represented. I\'ve confirmed no \"bulb\" related questions exist in `src/questions.js` after a grep search.\n\n\n**Identifying Image Relationships**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the user\'s provided images in context. I\'ve noted a cross-section of a valve, five sprinklers (A-E), a union fitting, a hex bushing, and a pipe nipple. The first image points to the packing of a valve, not a sprinkler bulb. Questions about bulb are not represented in the data. I\'m clarifying how each image relates to potential question types.\n\n\n**Revisiting Image Mapping**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the image assignments within the question data. The sixth image, a coupling fitting, is now under review in relation to question mapping. The user\'s request for \"identify the parts of the bulb\" seems to align more closely with \"identify the part of the valve\" in the data, which uses an image of a valve\'s packing. I need to ensure a correct mapping based on the user\'s intent.\n\n\n**Checking Image Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on verifying image display for \"Identify the valve\" and \"Identify the fire sprinkler\" questions. I\'ve re-examined the code and confirmed that the images are supposed to be rendered. I will now examine the filesystem for the image files. I\'m checking if the files are physically present in the expected location, or if their naming conventions or locations are different from what is specified in the data.\n\n\n"
