    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEjlBYhZVA0Y1r-g8dEHlmAg6aGxW0VklShZLdz0WZ1EyokkVrgmcXDtX91qgX02iRwmSDp0fhH4nbp5_NOznyjmB2kyNBvkhEYFJRy6I1tNuXtRejFcIP3FUMScEeYih8IruO4mGLJZy39zgSoO37JhWjQqEVbYochA7yfVGuK-Cj6W4nY9uTNL-cYjhBmJhrVGWHrXWk="
      title: "ifanpiping.com"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGMTcWuymYExTmgiHV0SbcYApbELReLJVXNYKGKP-dX2d6NK1qFUbMVPi5Co3BKBEC0CItSduNyOFpVrg7fGMX5KOWPbazgicExlpoMNVrAMKOusLv4jNB7ThRSN1w8_hy6AbC9KQw="
      title: "bessercast.com"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEdPHX2vihdpW9jTkxUL5V4oDKn7uA_tY9rS_4RDgmO_fzroA1iZ-71UTNgCMp16zJ-0if3DgzEjc5o1OjWFd53OfXEwyYh9styLy5LNDm9Mts1x0iqfnmxaQUtUQGLRUHdAc-Thjxke15OohtVXTtEQV94QBgiqw2Fk7LWdvcVPo6m-zVY-y45HAEreQ=="
      title: "meritbrass.com"
    }
    summary: "When referring to a \"bulb\" in the context of sprinkler or plumbing systems, the most common interpretation relates to the heat-sensitive glass bulb found in fire sprinkler heads. These bulbs are integral to the sprinkler\'s activation mechanism. In plumbing, while not commonly referred to as a \"bulb\" itself, thermal expansion relief valves perform a similar temperature-sensing function.\n\n**Parts of a Fire Sprinkler Head (featuring a glass bulb):**\nA fire sprinkler head is comprised of several key parts that work together to detect heat and release water:\n*   **Heat-Sensitive Element (Glass Bulb)**: This is the \"bulb\" itself, typically a sealed glass capsule filled with a glycerin-based liquid[1][2][3]. The color of the liquid indicates the sprinkler\'s activation temperature[4][2]. When exposed to sufficient heat from a fire, the liquid expands, causing the glass bulb to burst[5][1][2]. Some sprinkler heads use a fusible link instead of a glass bulb[5][6][1].\n*   **Plug/Sealing Assembly**: This component holds back the water within the sprinkler and piping network. It is released when the glass bulb breaks, allowing water to flow[5][1][4][2][3].\n*   **Deflector**: A fan-shaped or flat metal plate located at the bottom of the sprinkler head. Its purpose is to disperse the released water in a specific spray pattern to cover a designated area[5][6][1][4][2][3].\n*   **Frame**: This is the metal structure that holds all the parts of the sprinkler head together[5][6][1][4][3].\n*   **Orifice (Opening)**: The opening through which water flows once the plug is released. Its size impacts the sprinkler\'s flow rate[6][4][3].\n*   **Inlet Connection/Threading**: The threaded end of the sprinkler head that connects it to the water supply piping[6][4].\n*   **Cage**: Often included for protection, the cage surrounds the sprinkler head to prevent damage that could lead to malfunction[5].\n*   **Escutcheon**: A decorative plate that can be installed with some sprinkler heads for a finished appearance, especially with pendant sprinklers[1][3].\n\n**\"Bulb\" in Plumbing (Thermal Expansion Relief Valves):**\nIn plumbing, the term \"bulb\" is less common as a standalone part. However, some plumbing components, particularly **thermal expansion relief valves (TERVs)**, incorporate a heat-sensitive element that functions similarly to a sprinkler bulb to manage pressure due to thermal expansion in hot water systems[7][8]. These valves are safety devices that open to release excess pressure and water when the system\'s temperature or pressure reaches a predefined limit, preventing damage to the water heater or system[7][8]. While not explicitly called a \"bulb,\" the temperature-sensing mechanism in these valves serves a comparable purpose to the glass bulb in a fire sprinkler head[7]. Other types of valves in plumbing, such as ball valves, gate valves, and butterfly valves, control water flow but do not typically feature a \"bulb\" component[9][10][11][12][13].\n\nSources:\n[1] [koorsen.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFaRnab97op0YTbvJjNv3KhAC6PptJrNNCuP3Eh0RGc_CquFCNzoyTw3X7COptImX3-9DWXDEse6oR72yG4MJMjh0HR4wLjwo_JWggRG03pNLoqd-9S5ogvQ1g6SQmC2o7kDm8DL6ztp9QevifCmU62CJeskn9DPrQllEp2vvMUJlbeAQFQqsU=)\n[2] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE4yFHaXssckNsGKRol7AhxjBkvLZ9S_ebZVh5l-dC7-iR32hFVY7Dzh1qCkVyC0spauNNiP9__hDbStMUxK4_XiwAatLHZeQAQv8Zq8pI5S1MtnPkmSSzoVWHWDCsfTLCP85qElQ==)\n[3] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFu5yAdrRzNr6kT5TKLNzSUarxlOVKx3u80UUj0uNiNedeUsAvMj6iE3C9_ey3BzyOQY0FCNgB7AzPotNjMXi0MCSinpSy_tkT4oGpcuQX_-Z4NXQf5VkPYbzjRhkFFu-VBrHGuPg==)\n[4] [meyerfire.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHfUgkfNiui92now9wF4amV0F9psvx9udUTaITWSUyiQfZe_vJ6T2zYFTGagJ3PUMj82EAx6vjzIaa1dqlzZFOoyMqji4TmtWLP0UD_1oxXiCxQDnfHEfnwvU3VQrI3KzWCpORzA7yRyTYs1Wz1Pc5E4oOArckMfg==)\n[5] [rcscorp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFG4NkRWRQP8Ojw1SoqM33ly7PscGaF0gylfKqRDE78vCa8WsyBh9OA-Yl0BgVhjB7fG10a0Q1e6W2NhEqff1ovWV3jaViEqwsRAeKRikllKrFhOVaOHyCD83MoQjYaPjtHOVwzUFDDTEsY47Ru2aBCK-9TAdLlemuk5PONi3w=)\n[6] [fluidtechpiping.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHnJhSkcr3hrDZJcLF1yWhu4oSFcV-v04whR9Qub7S0NDaOxpi_nutB8VPJvcF_8Sxddl7UgmC9-vSNkqdgBC-hu-ckJltQRVbGqPXGrA0LWC4Rp5Q3a6Je5rBj8UOuPMl22dBEvmvMq6Hu1tgonZi5P-RToRKi_n_FXey78mIpU_mmpLuVHuQWWzQhDMk3DOfM2llyiqo=)\n[7] [abilityengineering.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFXB6I3m4sn5CaCz6B3Gdtl767U69E7J49ETSpvuyFGYfu5APRIsI6dDmFnzQQrmE7diXYJkbv9OkjmoRaWAy1SvREhnhFzIEvKhwf9ljYdqWQCFEeC4JB4iFIhF1y27BFKC-vcS7Xv44SE68DoHeV3upITxNOseGZ_MWTVgngr1_0SlLNW3xFqL5-9AM_WzYu0SFeRHk8=)\n[8] [redwhitevalvecorp.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE5Gd98OlviC32xMLK6zvstWtPQ5jSkUvyaWh5RnQp72UKbRk1nAyosZ3siK9-4HlazQMyme4EqH3jIPAXMocyHc4rcHlmjY3wZZzmA4E8IhiuGURwrVp3eVw0P_bWWhsl4bPSMgSGI9DOXCIknXRtSRy32Tn2qRQ==)\n[9] [youngarchitect.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFxiWVkT1XBORXLoF-zjOgerrAgGbOQ6pm39FpMK8zSk4Nc_LUle92ofg1x0s5lPQhJQxWF7Y56OWwaWXMO6zbbwMBj200zcEMVDpZ-85G8Ul3O6xHXVxA_LZScyO51MkykZPt6In6g4Eg0i1YKBw==)\n[10] [tameson.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_63zErx8IvkNIX4jB0ALzVGldwSSp9b61RUt32icNveUSS9sVD--Xbga3M0NRhMQof8IWXoSVbe8WjhJMeFyqQmmzdhjFUNx78uZf-rAlykBcadZ5irM1kckNaofX29qGyfOnSp-zYHiq7Q==)\n[11] [ifanpiping.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEjlBYhZVA0Y1r-g8dEHlmAg6aGxW0VklShZLdz0WZ1EyokkVrgmcXDtX91qgX02iRwmSDp0fhH4nbp5_NOznyjmB2kyNBvkhEYFJRy6I1tNuXtRejFcIP3FUMScEeYih8IruO4mGLJZy39zgSoO37JhWjQqEVbYochA7yfVGuK-Cj6W4nY9uTNL-cYjhBmJhrVGWHrXWk=)\n[12] [bessercast.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redi