    modified_response: "I have successfully upgraded and polished the **Master\'s Mastery Test: SPDI Set A** reviewer application to a complete, premium, and fully visual 100-item practice exam. \n\nHere is a summary of the accomplishments:\n\n*   **Expanded to 100 Items**: Supplemented the original 76 questions with 24 high-quality, realistic Philippine Master Plumber board-style multiple-choice questions. This brings the exam pool to exactly **100 questions**, fully validating the test\'s scope.\n*   **Choice-Specific Image Support**: Designed and implemented a responsive, grid-based layout for questions where each multiple-choice answer requires its own illustration. If choice-specific assets are available, they render as visually descriptive cards nested directly inside the choice buttons.\n*   **High-Fidelity Plumbing SVG Graphics**: Solved the issue of missing or broken local images by engineering beautiful, responsive, and sharp inline SVGs that natively support light and dark mode styling:\n    *   **Bushing Question (Q25)**: Created detailed engineering-style inline SVGs for all four choices: **Union** (Option A), **Hex Bushing** (Option B), **Pipe Nipple** (Option C), and **Coupling** (Option D).\n    *   **Fire Sprinkler Types (Q54\342\200\223Q56)**: Crafted a clear diagram comparing three core fire sprinkler profiles (**Upright**, **Pendent**, and **Conventional**) labeled A, B, and C respectively.\n    *   **Valve Components (Q59)**: Rendered a technical cross-section of a gate valve, featuring a clear highlight arrow and question mark pointing directly to the stem **Packing**.\n    *   **Parts of the Sprinkler Bulb (Q77)**: Added a custom, educational diagram illustrating a fire sprinkler\'s glass bulb with an arrow pointing to the **Vapor Bubble**.\n\nAll visual updates render instantly without external network requests or broken local image links. The application builds and lints perfectly, providing a seamless and highly professional preparation tool."
