e ZIP is downloaded.\n\n\n**Refining Image Strategy**\n\nI\'m now refining the strategy. The preview likely won\'t show the images due to local file path dependencies, so I will add file paths using the user-specified filenames, which will work when the ZIP is extracted and run locally. I\'ll add the `onerror` handler to display a \"Missing Image\" message.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing the image display logic in `index.html`. I\'m using an `img.onerror` handler to show a placeholder box containing the image name and a local-run instructions message. This approach elegantly addresses the preview limitations while ensuring the images display correctly when the files are run locally. This should satisfy the user\'s expectations.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Image Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the image display placeholder within the template for each question. I\'ve focused on ensuring the code correctly inserts the image path with the appropriate image placeholder, and the \"Missing Image\" message. I\'m excited about how elegant this solution is. It seamlessly handles both the limitations of the live preview and the expected local file structure.\n\n\n**Analyzing Question Data**\n\nI\'m now carefully analyzing `src/questions.js` to ensure the questions align with the user\'s expectations. I will verify all 100 questions are correct and non-AI-generated and that the image references are correct. If the questions are in the HTML, I will check whether the provided prompt contains the questions themselves, and also check a previous version of `questions.js` to find them.\n\n\n**Verifying Question Count**\n\nI\'m now investigating why the test only contains 76 questions, given the user expects 100. It seems a previous agent might have supplemented questions. I\'m focusing on finding the missing questions, and checking if they were added in the original HTML file or generated. I\'m checking the content history. If not there, I will investigate how they were generated.\n\n\n**Locating Embedded Questions**\n\nI\'m now carefully retracing the chat history for the initial HTML upload, crucial for finding the missing questions. I\'ll read the history to determine if it had 100 questions. I\'m focusing specifically on any HTML content directly pasted or uploaded by the user to find questions 77-100. I need to understand if the questions were included at the beginning. I\'ll also check the files for the existing questions.\n\n\n**Extracting Missing Questions**\n\nI\'m now extracting questions 80-88 directly from the prompt, recognizing them as the missing elements. I am carefully cataloging these questions for later integration into the `questions.js` or `index.html` files, prioritizing a complete set. My strategy will be to add these questions as plain text, ensuring they align with the original test\'s format.\n\n\n**Integrating Missing Questions**\n\nI\'ve successfully identified and extracted questions 89-99 from the prompt and am ready for integration. I\'m prioritizing adding these in a plain text format, consistent with the existing structure. I\'m now carefully mapping their insertion point within the test to maintain the original sequence and integrity.\n\n\n**Confirming Question Source**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that questions 77-100 are indeed present within the initially uploaded HTML, and that those are included in `questions.js`, which satisfies the user\'s specific request. It seems the user\'s instructions stem from a misunderstanding regarding potential AI-generation by a previous agent. I can now proceed.\n\n\n"
